{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Conversation Ledger\n2\t\n3\tDurable, attributable records of visible coding-agent conversations, stored in\n4\tyour repository as git notes.\n5\t\n6\t`cledger` (also installed as `conversation-ledger`) is a small standalone\n7\tutility in the unix tradition: it appends immutable JSONL evidence events to\n8\t`refs/notes/conversation-ledger`, anchored to the commit you were on when the\n9\tconversation happened. Records ride the commit DAG — merge a branch and its\n10\tconversations come along, and squash-merged branches are re-anchored onto the\n11\tsquash commit — never touch your working tree or `git status`, and\n12\tride your normal `git push`/`git fetch` via an auto-installed, scan-gated\n13\tpre-push hook and fetch refspec (or explicitly, via `cledger sync`).\n14\t\n15\tConversation Ledger is the neutral foundation of a small ecosystem:\n16\t\n17\t- `conversation-ledger` stores normalized, provenance-preserving conversation evidence.\n18\t- `turnbridge` records and transfers visible conversations between coding CLIs.\n19\t- `intent-recall` later retrieves evidence to help agents reason about original and superseded intent.\n20\t\n21\tThe ledger itself never summarizes, ranks, or interprets. It stores what was\n22\tvisibly said, by whom, against which commit — nothing more.\n23\t\n24\t## Install\n25\t\n26\t```sh\n27\tgit clone https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger\n28\tcd conversation-ledger && npm install && npm link   # npm publish coming later\n29\tcledger install all    # hook capture into Claude Code + Codex CLI\n30\t```","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SJnSUhYFByyoh7ZfqFuNmP","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","dirty_fingerprint":"3842c428ed4e1c949a7fc520cd5ab72676a40911feeabf7c7d455ce763117115","head":"d87dc8457e6a42db0c74f287e08efe5f4a2bf83