{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Technical design\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** implemented in v0.1; format may still evolve until v1.\n4\t\n5\t## Scope\n6\t\n7\tConversation Ledger defines a canonical append-only event format plus a local,\n8\tgit-backed storage protocol. It preserves exact visible content while staying\n9\tout of the working tree. Transport is on by default and rides normal git use:\n10\ta pre-push hook pushes the ledger ref alongside `git push` (scan-gated), and\n11\ta fetch refspec stages the remote's ref for lazy merge at read time (see\n12\t\"Transport\"); `cledger sync` remains the explicit path and the fallback when\n13\thooks are declined.\n14\t\n15\t## Canonical objects\n16\t\n17\tAn `EvidenceEvent` is immutable and has:\n18\t\n19\t- `id`: `ev1-` + sha256 of the event's *identity subset* — the durable,\n20\t  source-determined fields (`kind`, `occurred_at`, `actor.type/id`,\n21\t  `producer.source/session_id`, `conversation`, `media_type`, `content`,\n22\t  `links`). Volatile provenance (`recorded_at`, `context`, `raw`,\n23\t  `producer.tool/version`) is excluded, so re-scanning the same source\n24\t  material always yields the same id: capture is idempotent by construction,\n25\t  and the id doubles as the content hash that makes mutation detectable.\n26\t- `schema` version (`conversation-ledger/v1`);\n27\t- `kind`: `conversation_turn`, `decision`, `document`, `annotation`,\n28\t  `redaction`, or `supersession` — an open string; unknown kinds are stored\n29\t  verbatim so downstream tools can extend without a schema release;\n30\t- `occurred_at` (from the source) and `recorded_at` (at append) timestamps;\n31\t- `actor` (human/agent/system + identity) and `producer` (capture tool,\n32\t  source system, native session id) provenance; adapters stamp human turns\n33\t  with the identity a commit made right now would be authored under,\n34\t  resolved by git itself (`g