{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"30\t```\n31\t\n32\t`cledger install` adds `Stop`/`SessionEnd` hooks to `~/.claude/settings.json`\n33\tand a `Stop` hook (plus `features.hooks = true`) to `~/.codex/config.toml`,\n34\tbacking both up first. From then on, every completed turn in any git\n35\trepository is captured automatically, in the same universal format. Capture is\n36\tidempotent — events are content-derived, so re-scanning a transcript never\n37\tduplicates.\n38\t\n39\tTwo one-time activation notes: Claude Code reads hooks at session start, so\n40\tcapture begins with your next session; Codex requires you to trust new hooks\n41\tinteractively — open `codex`, run `/hooks`, and approve the `cledger hook\n42\tcodex` command once. Missed turns are never lost either way: `cledger capture\n43\t<source> --transcript PATH` backfills any native transcript, idempotently.\n44\t\n45\t## Use\n46\t\n47\t```sh\n48\tcledger log                     # events on the current branch (via commit reachability)\n49\tcledger log --all --json        # every event, as JSONL for jq & friends\n50\tcledger conversations           # sessions touching this branch\n51\tcledger show claude-code:3f9a   # replay one conversation in order\n52\tcledger export > ledger.jsonl   # lossless dump, incl. source-native payloads\n53\tcledger sync                    # explicit fetch/merge/push of the ledger ref\n54\tcledger re-anchor               # what did the remote squash away? (--apply to map it)\n55\techo '{\"kind\":\"decision\",...}' | cledger append   # any tool can write events\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\t## Sharing (transport)\n59\t\n60\tThe ledger travels with normal git use, no extra commands:\n61\t\n62\t- **Push**: the first capture in a repo installs a `pre-push` hook (chaining\n63\t  safely onto any existing shell hook; backing off with a warning when\n64\t  `core.hooksPath`/husky owns the hooks). On `git push` it pushes the ledger\n65\t  ref alongside, gated by the secret scan. A finding holds back **only the\n66\t  ledger** — your code push proceeds — unless you opt into\n67\t  `{\"transport\": {\"strict\": true}}`, which aborts the whole push.\n68\t- **Fetch**: the same first capture adds a fetch refspec on `origin`, so\n69\t  `git fetch`/`git pull` stages teammates' events; any read command\n70\t  (`cledger log`, `show`, ...) folds them in via the conflict-free\n71\t  `cat_sort_uniq` union. The local ref is never force-overwritten.\n72\t- **Opting out**: `{\"transport\": {\"hook\": false, \"fetchRefspec\": false}}` in\n73\t  `.cledger.json` or `~/.config/cledger/config.json`, or just delete the\n74\t  marked block from `.git/hooks/pre-push`. `cledger sync` always works\n75\t  explicitly either way.\n76\t\n77\tIf git has no author identity configured (`user.email` unset), human turns\n78\tare recorded unattributed; `cledger install` warns about this. cledger uses\n79\tthe same identity a commit would be authored under (config or environment)","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XcQZx3E154PUtENGRMf9an","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","dirty_fingerprint":"3842c428ed4e1c949a7fc520cd5ab72676a40911feeabf7c7d455ce763117115","head":"d87dc8457e6a42db0c74f287e08efe5f4a2bf839","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:4e61425c-e72a-4a89-8190-ba7cfb584d78","seq":175},"id":"ev1-4e94abb2017cad21069014005ccfafdb46d99839d64af106dbd4038f6d0b7882","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-27T05:21:37.429Z","producer":{"session_id":"4e61425c-e72a-4a89-8190-ba7cfb584d78","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.11.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"30\t```\n31\t\n32\t`cledger install` adds `Stop`/`SessionEn