{"actor":{"id":"claude-sonnet-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"**Answers to your two questions:**\n\n1. **Outside a repo:** Safe, already handled. Both hook entrypoints (`runClaudeCodeHook`/`runCodexHook`) check `findRepo(cwd)` and return immediately if it's null — no files, no state, nothing written anywhere outside a git repo.\n2. **Subfolder of a repo:** Also already handled — `findRepo` calls `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, which is git's own upward directory walk, so a session started three folders deep still resolves to the right repo root.\n\n**What I added — per-repo disable flag (v0.11.0):**\n\nDrop this in a repo's `.cledger.json`:\n```json\n{\"enabled\": false}\n```\n\nIt's gated centrally in `appendEvents` (`src/store.ts`), the single choke point every write path already goes through — hook capture, manual `cledger append`, and `cledger capture --transcript` backfill all become clean no-ops before the ledger ref or transport is ever touched. Reads (`log`/`show`/`export`) are unaffected, so existing history stays visible; it only stops new events from being written. Same merge precedence as everything else in the config (repo's `.cledger.json` wins over the global `~/.config/cledger/config.json`, so you could also flip the global default off and opt specific repos back in).\n\nAdded a test (`store.test.ts`) confirming it's a total no-op, updated the README, bumped `package.json` to 0.11.0 to match the repo's convention of pairing shipped features with a version bump. Full suite passes (136/136, 1 pre-existing skip). Nothing committed — all changes are in the working tree for you to review.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","dirty_fingerprint":"3842c428ed4e1c949a7fc520cd5ab72676a40911feeabf7c7d455ce763117115","head":"d87dc8457e6a42db0c74f287e08efe5f4a2bf839","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude